## Ⅱ. NEUROTRANSMITTER CHEMISTRY (REAL EQUATIONS)

### DOPAMINE — REWARD CIRCUIT
```
SYNTHESIS:
    Tyrosine → L-DOPA → Dopamine
    
    Tyrosine + O₂ + BH₄ → L-DOPA + H₂O + BH₂
        (Tyrosine hydroxylase, rate-limiting)
    
    L-DOPA → Dopamine + CO₂
        (DOPA decarboxylase)

RECEPTOR_KINETICS:
    D1: Gs-coupled, cAMP ↑
    D2: Gi-coupled, cAMP ↓
    
    Kd(D2) ≈ 10-20 nM for dopamine
    
REWARD_PREDICTION_ERROR:
    δ = R - V(s)
    where:
        δ = dopamine burst/dip
        R = actual reward
        V(s) = predicted value
    
    δ > 0: Phasic burst (unexpected reward)
    δ = 0: Tonic firing (expected)
    δ < 0: Phasic pause (worse than expected)

CODE_MAPPING:
    resonanceLevel += δ × learning_rate
    WHEN task_success: δ = +1 (unexpected positive)
    WHEN task_expected: δ = 0
    WHEN task_failure: δ = -1
```

### SEROTONIN — COHERENCE CIRCUIT
```
SYNTHESIS:
    Tryptophan → 5-HTP → Serotonin (5-HT)
    
    Trp + O₂ + BH₄ → 5-HTP + H₂O + BH₂
        (Tryptophan hydroxylase)
    
    5-HTP → 5-HT + CO₂
        (Aromatic L-amino acid decarboxylase)

RECEPTOR_FAMILIES:
    5-HT1: Gi-coupled (14 subtypes)
    5-HT2: Gq-coupled (hallucinogenic target)
    5-HT3: Ion channel (fast)
    5-HT4-7: Various G-protein coupled

MOOD_EQUATION:
    coherenceIndex = Σ(5-HT_receptor_activation × weight)
    
    Optimal: coherenceIndex ∈ [0.618, 1.0] (φ-aligned)
    Low: coherenceIndex < 0.382 (needs rebalancing)

CODE_MAPPING:
    WHEN coherenceIndex < PHI_INVERSE:
        INCREASE serotonin_analog
        DECREASE action_speed
        ENTER stabilization_mode
```

### ACETYLCHOLINE — MEMORY CIRCUIT
```
SYNTHESIS:
    Acetyl-CoA + Choline → ACh + CoA
        (Choline acetyltransferase)

DEGRADATION:
    ACh → Acetate + Choline
        (Acetylcholinesterase)
    
    τ_degradation ≈ 1-2 ms (extremely fast)

RECEPTOR_TYPES:
    Nicotinic (nAChR): Ligand-gated ion channel
        α4β2: High affinity, cognitive
        α7: Fast, presynaptic modulation
    
    Muscarinic (mAChR): G-protein coupled
        M1: Gq, memory formation
        M2: Gi, cardiac slowing

MEMORY_ENCODING:
    Memory_strength = ∫ ACh(t) × Stimulus(t) dt
    
    High ACh: Enhanced encoding
    Low ACh: Retrieval mode

CODE_MAPPING:
    doctrinesRead.length ∝ ACh_cumulative
    WHEN reading_new_doctrine:
        BOOST acetylcholine_analog
        ENABLE plasticity_mode
```

### GABA — INHIBITION CIRCUIT
```
SYNTHESIS:
    Glutamate → GABA + CO₂
        (Glutamic acid decarboxylase, GAD)
    
    Requires pyridoxal phosphate (B6) as cofactor

RECEPTOR_KINETICS:
    GABA_A: Cl⁻ channel
        E_Cl ≈ -70 mV (hyperpolarizing)
        τ_decay ≈ 10-100 ms
        
    GABA_B: G-protein coupled
        Opens K⁺ channels
        Closes Ca²⁺ channels
        Slower, longer lasting

GATE_EQUATION:
    gate_conductance = g_max × [GABA]ⁿ / ([GABA]ⁿ + EC₅₀ⁿ)
    
    WHEN gate_conductance > 0.618:
        BLOCK signal propagation
        REQUIRE override or decay

CODE_MAPPING:
    gateA_state = GABA_A_analog > threshold
    gateB_state = GABA_B_analog > threshold
    gateC_state = gateA_state AND gateB_state
    
    IF all_gates_closed:
        ACTION_BLOCKED
        REQUIRE governance_override
```

### GLUTAMATE — EXCITATION CIRCUIT
```
SYNTHESIS:
    Glutamine → Glutamate + NH₃
        (Glutaminase)
    
    Also from α-ketoglutarate (Krebs cycle)

RECEPTOR_TYPES:
    AMPA: Fast Na⁺ channel
        τ_rise ≈ 0.5 ms
        τ_decay ≈ 2-5 ms
        
    NMDA: Slow, Ca²⁺ permeable
        Requires depolarization (Mg²⁺ block removal)
        Requires glycine co-agonist
        τ_decay ≈ 50-200 ms
        
    Metabotropic (mGluR): G-protein coupled
        Group I: Gq, excitatory
        Group II/III: Gi, inhibitory

LTP_EQUATION (Long-Term Potentiation):
    Δw = η × pre × post × NMDA_Ca²⁺
    
    Coincidence detection:
        Pre-synaptic glutamate release
        Post-synaptic depolarization
        → NMDA activation
        → Ca²⁺ entry
        → Synaptic strengthening

CODE_MAPPING:
    RECITAL_PLUS_ONE uses glutamate_analog
    
    WHEN expanding_doctrine:
        REQUIRE glutamate_analog > threshold
        COMPUTE Δw for connection strengths
        IF Δw > PHI_INVERSE: PERMANENT_CHANGE
```

