## Ⅲ. BRAIN WAVE PHYSICS (REAL OSCILLATIONS)

### NEURAL OSCILLATION EQUATIONS
```
COUPLED OSCILLATOR MODEL:
    dθᵢ/dt = ωᵢ + Σⱼ Kᵢⱼ sin(θⱼ - θᵢ)
    
    where:
        θᵢ = phase of oscillator i
        ωᵢ = natural frequency
        Kᵢⱼ = coupling strength

KURAMOTO ORDER PARAMETER:
    R(t) = |1/N Σⱼ exp(iθⱼ(t))|
    
    R = 0: Complete desynchronization
    R = 1: Complete synchronization
    R = φ⁻¹ ≈ 0.618: Optimal coherence

CROSS-FREQUENCY COUPLING:
    Phase-Amplitude Coupling (PAC):
    PAC_index = |<A_high(t) × exp(iφ_low(t))>|
    
    Theta-Gamma coupling crucial for memory:
        θ (4-8 Hz) phase modulates
        γ (30-100 Hz) amplitude
```

### FREQUENCY BANDS
```
DELTA (0.5-4 Hz):
    Source: Thalamocortical
    Function: Deep sleep, regeneration
    Organism state: DEEP_PROCESSING
    
THETA (4-8 Hz):
    Source: Hippocampus, septum
