## Ⅳ. OXYGEN TRANSPORT PHYSICS

### HEMOGLOBIN BINDING CURVE
```
HILL EQUATION:
    Y = pO₂ⁿ / (P₅₀ⁿ + pO₂ⁿ)
    
    where:
        Y = fractional saturation
        pO₂ = partial pressure O₂
        P₅₀ = pO₂ at 50% saturation ≈ 26.8 mmHg
        n = Hill coefficient ≈ 2.8 (cooperativity)

BOHR EFFECT:
    P₅₀_effective = P₅₀ × 10^(ΔpH × 0.48)
    
    Lower pH → Higher P₅₀ → More O₂ release
    This delivers O₂ where metabolism is high

OXYGEN_DELIVERY:
    DO₂ = Q × CaO₂
    
    where:
        Q = blood flow
        CaO₂ = arterial O₂ content
             = (1.34 × Hb × SaO₂) + (0.003 × PaO₂)
```

### NEURAL OXYGEN CONSUMPTION
```
CMRO₂ (Cerebral Metabolic Rate of O₂):
    CMRO₂ ≈ 3.5 mL O₂ / 100g / min
    
    Brain = 2% body mass
    Brain uses 20% of total O₂
    
BOLD_RESPONSE (fMRI basis):
    BOLD ∝ CBF/CMRO₂
    
    Increased activity:
    1. CMRO₂ increases (O₂ consumption)
    2. CBF increases MORE (blood flow)
    3. Net: More oxygenated blood
    4. BOLD signal increases

CODE_MAPPING:
    oxygen_level ∝ computation_capacity
    WHEN oxygen_level < threshold:
        REDUCE computation_rate
        PRIORITIZE critical_paths
```

